KG42.register("edges-ea7857e42e5025d8376e39d1",{"id":"S-0c2bbafd311d22b6","source":"KG40-45833afd23977831","type":"links","target":"KG31-589dd70d32471060","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["23-hierarchical_market_structure"],"assertions":[{"id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001","paper":"23-hierarchical_market_structure","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","rule_ref":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R004","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG40-45833afd23977831","target":"KG31-589dd70d32471060","source_occurrence_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","source_unit_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"DNEM in the proposed hierarchical WEM-DNEM electricity market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"39672d32867e7357eda3c22c507d24cdf68d0c3b59a87cbe9d2dcead6e649c82","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"In this reported case, the LA's 15 MW DNEM award at iteration 204 occurs under the stated condition that the DNEM MCP exceeds the WEM LMP at its bus. Scope: Case 1 numerical trajectory: higher microgrid marginal costs and no wholesale-market congestion; DNEM award at iteration 204. Condition: The DNEM MCP is higher than the WEM LMP at the LA bus. The DNO performs DNEM clearing and provides the LA's awarded dispatch. Scope: Distribution-network electricity market clearing in the proposed hierarchical mechanism. DNEM clearing minimizes the operational cost of the distribution network. Scope: DNEM clearing objective in formulation (19)–(22). Microgrid generation plus LA imports must equal total distribution-network demand plus LA exports. Scope: DNEM clearing load-balance constraint (20). Awarded microgrid generation and each LA's imported power must remain within their respective specified lower and upper bounds. Scope: DNEM clearing constraints (21)–(22). The DNEM clearing model assumes that electricity delivery is not limited by distribution-line congestion. Scope: Distribution-network delivery assumption in the DNEM clearing formulation. The DNEM import branch sets the LA's current import upper bound to the import-minus-export quantity at reference index k-1+v and fixes its current export quantity to zero. Scope: Single-LA iterative algorithm, DNEM import branch at step d before clearing at step f. Condition: At step c, P^{imp,k-1+v}_{l} > P^{exp,k-1+v}_{l}. The DNEM export branch retains the import upper bound and export quantity from reference index k-1+v for the current clearing iteration. Scope: Single-LA iterative algorithm, DNEM export branch at step e before clearing at step f. Condition: At step c, inequality (47) does not hold: the import quantity at reference index k-1+v does not exceed the export quantity at that index.","target_definition":"The DNO, as local market coordinator, provides the DNEM market clearing price. Scope: DNEM in the proposed hierarchical WEM-DNEM electricity market.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The DNO, as local market coordinator, provides the DNEM market clearing price. Scope: DNEM in the proposed hierarchical WEM-DNEM electricity market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E005","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. Introduction","anchor_text":"composed of these markets. Here, each market participant bids in associated electricity market, whil","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Fig. 1 shows the proposed hierarchical market structure that composed of these markets. Here, each market participant bids in associated electricity market, while each LA is an intermediate agent that participates in both markets to address the synergy of the two markets. The LA bids in the WEM and presents the awarded dispatch in the DNEM as demand on its bus in the WEM. The ISO clears the market and provide the awarded dispatch for the LA and LMP at the LAs bus. The LA bids in the DNEM and presents the awarded dispatch in the WEM as demand on its bus in the DNEM. The DNO clears the market and provide the awarded dispatch for the LA and the market clearing price (MCP) of the market."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"DNEM in the proposed hierarchical WEM-DNEM electricity market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]},"paper_scope_note":"The interface between WEM and DNEM is retained; the two LA roles and the 15 MW revenue in Case 1 cannot be treated as general rules for the whole market."}}],"assertion_ids":["23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001"]});
